b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ HARNESS POSING reposed;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE author: implementation-algol-60, an agent (Claude Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE precursor seen: no;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE idioms: the Revised Report on ALGOL 60 (1962) for blocks and arrays (5.2), procedures (5.4), the for statement with step-until and while elements (4.6) and conditional statements (4.5), the X1 system's input and output procedures read, print, PRINTTEXT and NLCR, as the harness README gives them (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.1) and its own X1 programs cite them (Kruseman Aretz 2003, chapter 7), and the X1 compiler's representation, with underlined reserved words and the operator symbols (harness README, 2.1), the effect stub emit bound as printing (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.5), and the observe block of the harness README example X01 (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.8);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ CONSTANTS a line 1: F f1 ... fF c, the number of facts of pick, the value of each fact, in order, and then c, the integer of x at least c;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ P11a. One stage, a query for any one outcome: pick(x) and x at least c and emit(x), in that order. pick is given by its facts: each fact, in order, gives x a value, and the conjuncts after pick are carried out on it in order. The query asks for one answer, so the facts are tried only until one passes the whole conjunction. An answer, and the entry emitted, is x alone, its digits printed with no spaces;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ n, cap, m, i, code, k, j, nf, c, xv, cur;
  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ ok;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a̲r̲r̲a̲y̲ fv[1:1000], pk[1:1000];

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ num(v);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ v; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ v;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: an integer, a minus sign if it is negative and then its decimal digits, with no spaces;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ d;
    i̲f̲ v < 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`-'); num(-v) e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      i̲f̲ v ≥ 10 t̲h̲e̲n̲ num(v ÷ 10);
      d := v - v ÷ 10 × 10;
      i̲f̲ d = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`0') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`1') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`2')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`3') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 4 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`4') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 5 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`5')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 6 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`6') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 7 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`7') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 8 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`8')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(`9')
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ num;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ emit(v);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ v; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ v;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the effect stub emit(v) of the harness, bound as printing;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[emit]'); num(v); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/emit]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲ emit;

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: the instance line, and the one message, which poses stage 1;
  n := read; cap := read; m := read;
  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ m d̲o̲ code := read;
  code := read; k := read;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the stage's constants: pick's facts, and c;
  nf := read;
  f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ nf d̲o̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ fv[j] := read; pk[j] := 0 e̲n̲d̲;
  c := read;

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the query: pick(x) and x at least c and emit(x), in that order, until one x passes;
  ok := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲; cur := 0;
  f̲o̲r̲ j := 0 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ ¬ok ∧ cur < nf d̲o̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    cur := cur + 1; pk[cur] := pk[cur] + 1;
    xv := fv[cur];
    i̲f̲ xv ≥ c t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      emit(xv);
      ok := t̲r̲u̲e̲
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲;

  i̲f̲ ok t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[answer]'); num(xv); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/answer]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ observe: the value of x, and the facts of pick tried;
  PRINTTEXT(`[observe]');
  i̲f̲ ¬ok t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`no solution'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  i̲f̲ ok t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[bind x]'); num(xv); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`facts of pick tried: '); num(cur); PRINTTEXT(` of '); num(nf); NLCR;
  f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ nf d̲o̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[operations pick/'); num(j); PRINTTEXT(` '); print(pk[j]); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/observe]'); NLCR; PRINTTEXT(`[end]') e̲n̲d̲
e̲n̲d̲
